[Music]  hi everyone my name is nari Seoul and  today we're going to go over some ways  to sound like Claude Debussy now of  course it goes without saying that to  cover the details of his genius in a  video like this is pretty absurd but  here just a few practical ways that help  me understand his music and also allow  me to imitate at least the surface layer  of his style let's first take the melody  and add more space around the notes to  create an atmospheric vibe  [Music]  next let's add in our pated harp light  cascades accompanied with a resonant  bass line that often accentuates a  perfect fifth at the bottom linger on  tonal centers and generally avoid using  functional cadences  [Music]  an example of this is to use cores with  tritones in them such as dominant chords  without resolving them  [Music]  make use of Tremeloes to add tension  [Music]  include a lot of rhythmic variation in a  fluid manner  and also use spaced-out syncopated lines  to have an ambiguous sense of pulse at  times  [Music]  move chords and gestures with parallel  movement  [Music]  you scale such as the whole tone and  pentatonic scales as well as different  types of modes  [Music]  also include bell-like rings that add to  the atmosphere of the music  [Music]  and last but not least used textures and  Tambor's that create an air of ambience  and an imaginative mood  [Music]  and without further ado here's happy  birthday in the style of called Debussy  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  so I hope you enjoy that thanks so much  for watching and if you're interested in  the PDF of this version of happy  birthday it'll be available on my  website where you can also find my book  of modified Chopin exercises and other  sheet music anyway thanks again and I'll  see you in the next video  [Music]  you  [Music]

